      "sender": "dlloveras",
      "body": "inside surya_workshop2026/downstream_apps/test/experiments we have the creation and visualization of pooled running difference images.   In surya_workshop2026/downstream_apps/test/models/simple_baseline.py we are creating a logistic regression that aims to take advantage of the fact that waves are more prominent after pooling images.\n\nPooling the image with 32x32 pixels looks good, but I want my logistic regression to operate on scalars, not full images so I want to calculate the 32x32 pull of the running difference, take the absolute value of the outcome, averageit in space to collapse 4kx4k images into a scalar and then run the logistic regression.   Draft a plan to make the necessary changes to the model so that it woks this way.  Ask me any clarifying questions",
