pooled-map contrast, wave vs its matched no-wave control\")\nplot_task_1_1.py:150:        w = float(np.abs(wave[\"pooled_32\"]).max())\nplot_task_1_1.py:151:        n = float(np.abs(no_wave[\"pooled_32\"]).max())\nplot_task_1_1.py:152:        print(f\"  {event}: max|pooled| wave {w:.4f}  no wave {n:.4f}  ratio {w / n:.2f}\")\nrun_baseline_study.py:5:Everything here runs on the cached AIA193 running-difference features that\nrun_baseline_study.py:10:The model is exactly ``RunningDifferenceLogisticModel``: a 32x32 mean pool of\nrun_baseline_study.py:12:trained with BCE-with-logits. The cache is stored at pool kernel 8 and re-pooled here,\nrun_baseline_study.py:13:which is numerically identical (mean pooling composes over equal-sized blocks) and is what\nrun_baseline_study.py:14:makes the pooling sweep free.\nrun_baseline_study.py:18:1. **1.2 reproduction.** ``runs/wave_classification_baseline_running_diff/version_3``\nrun_baseline_study.py:63:    p.add_argument(\"--pool-kernels\", default=\"8,16,32,64,128\")\nrun_baseline_study.py:195:    base_kernel = int(data[\"pool_kernel\"])\nrun_baseline_study.py:198:        raise SystemExit(f\"cached pool kernel {base_kernel} does not divide {BASE_POOL}\")\nrun_baseline_study.py:201:        return wc.repool(data[f\"X_{split}\"], kernel // base_kernel)\nrun_baseline_study.py:207:          f\"(cached at kernel {base_kernel}, re-pooled by {factor} to {BASE_POOL})\")\nrun_baseline_study.py:215:        \"pool_kernel_cached\": base_kernel,\nrun_baseline_study.py:275:    # --- 4. pooling kernel ----------------------------------------------------\nrun_baseline_study.py:276:    pool_rows = []\nrun_baseline_study.py:277:    for kernel in [int(v) for v in args.pool_kernels.split(\",\")]:\nrun_baseline_study.py:279:            print(f\"[pool]  skipping kernel {kernel}: not reachable from the cached {base_kernel}\")\nrun_baseline_study.py:289:        pool_rows.append({\"pool_kernel\": kernel, \"side\": int(Xk.shape[1]),\nrun_baseline_study.