    \"## Running-difference baseline, same axes\", \"\",\nwave_common.py:22:3. **The running-difference feature.** ``RunningDifferenceLogisticModel`` computes it on\nwave_common.py:24:   it. ``pooled_running_difference()`` is the single definition both use, and\nwave_common.py:237:        subset_seed: Must match the seed the runs use, or the \"nested prefix\" is a different\nwave_common.py:451:# The running-difference feature\nwave_common.py:454:def pooled_running_difference(\nwave_common.py:457:    pool_kernel: int,\nwave_common.py:459:    \"\"\"AIA193 running difference (now - previous), mean-pooled.\nwave_common.py:465:    Mean pooling composes: pooling a ``pool_kernel=8`` map by a further factor of 4 is\nwave_common.py:466:    identical to pooling the original by 32, because every block is the same size. That\nwave_common.py:475:        pool_kernel: Mean-pool kernel size (and stride).\nwave_common.py:478:        ``(B, H // pool_kernel, W // pool_kernel)``.\nwave_common.py:481:    diff = x[:, -1] - x[:, 0]                              # now - previous\nwave_common.py:482:    pooled = torch.nn.functional.avg_pool2d(diff.unsqueeze(1), kernel_size=pool_kernel)\nwave_common.py:483:    return pooled.squeeze(1)\nwave_common.py:486:def repool(features: np.ndarray, factor: int) -> np.ndarray:\nwave_common.py:487:    \"\"\"Mean-pool cached feature maps by a further integer ``factor``.\nwave_common.py:491:        factor: Additional pooling factor; must divide ``S``.\nwave_common.py:500:        raise ValueError(f\"repool factor {factor} does not divide the {s}x{s} cached map.\")\nwave_visibility_scan.py:7:``[-12, 0]`` the positive sample's running difference therefore spans **+18 to +30 min**\nwave_visibility_scan.py:13:This script measures it. For each of a few events it extracts the AIA193 running\nwave_visibility_scan.py:14:difference at onset offsets +12, +24, +36 and +48 min and reports the contrast of the",
