            "raw_output": "7:``[-12, 0]`` the positive sample's running difference therefore spans **+18 to +30 min**\n14:difference at onset offsets +12, +24, +36 and +48 min and reports the contrast of the\n16:difference at ``-30 min``. Because the control comes from the same event an hour earlier,\n19:Three contrast statistics are reported, all computed on the solar disk only:\n24:* ``pooled_max`` \u2014 max \\\\|RD\\\\| of the 32x32-mean-pooled 128x128 map. This is the one that\n58:# The control window: the negative sample's own running difference, 30 min BEFORE onset.\n71:# 0.36 stops short of it on purpose. A static limb cancels in a running difference, but the\n73:# the difference (visible in the task 1.1 figures), and that ring would dominate the 99.9th\n79:def parse_args() -> argparse.Namespace:\n86:                   help=\"Draws the events from the same seeded pool the training runs use.\")\n93:def nearest_frame(stamps: np.ndarray, target: pd.Timestamp) -> \"pd.Timestamp | None\":\n105:    best = min(candidates, key=lambda j: abs(stamps[j] - target64))\n106:    if abs(stamps[best] - target64) > np.timedelta64(SNAP_TOLERANCE):\n111:def resolve_pair(stamps: np.ndarray, onset: pd.Timestamp, offset_min: int,\n113:    \"\"\"Resolve one running-difference pair for ``onset + offset_min``.\n117:    so the difference always spans exactly one step \u2014 which is what the model sees.\n129:def disk_mask(side: int) -> np.ndarray:\n136:def contrast_stats(rd: np.ndarray, mask: np.ndarray) -> dict:\n137:    \"\"\"Contrast statistics for one running-difference map, on-disk only.\"\"\"\n139:    pooled = wc.repool(np.where(mask, rd, 0.0)[None].astype(np.float32), 32)[0]\n141:        \"p999\": float(np.percentile(np.abs(on_disk), 99.9)),\n143:        \"pooled_max\": float(np.abs(pooled).max()),\n147:def load_signum_log_frame(dataset, timestamp) -> np.ndarray:\n148:    \"\"\"Return AIA193 at ``timestamp`` in **signum-log** space, shape ``(H, W)``.\n151:    features live in and the space the running difference is taken in during training, so a\n152:    contrast measured here is a contrast the model could actually use. ``transform_data``\n163:def main() -> None:\n182:    print(f\"[scan] train pool: {info.describe()}\")\n189:    step = pd.Timedelta(minutes=abs(cfg.data.time_delta_input_minutes[0]))\n201:            f\"No event has all {len(wanted)} running-difference pairs available within \"\n214:        control = contrast_stats(\n220:            signal = contrast_stats(\n233:                  f\"pooled snr {row['pooled_max_snr']:5.2f}\", flush=True)\n241:def report(df: pd.DataFrame, offsets: list[int]) -> None:\n243:    summary = df.groupby(\"offset_min\")[[\"p999_snr\", \"std_snr\", \"pooled_max_snr\"]].agg(\n252:    med = df.groupby(\"offset_min\")[\"pooled_max_snr\"].median()\n262:        \"median_pooled_snr_by_offset\": {int(k): float(v) for k, v in med.items()},\n264:        \"best_median_pooled_snr\": float(med.max()),\n265:        \"median_pooled_snr_at_catalog_offset_30\": at_30,\n268:            f\"Signal peaks at +{best_offset:.0f} min (median pooled SNR \"\n285:def plot(df: pd.DataFrame, med: pd.Series, x: pd.Series,\n294:        [\"p999_snr\", \"std_snr\", \"pooled_max_snr\"],\n295:        [\"99.9th pct of |RD|\", \"std of RD\", \"max |RD| of the 128x128 pooled map\"],\n309:    fig.suptitle(\"Running-difference contrast vs where the positive sample is taken \"",
