            "raw_output": "configs/config_wave_full.yaml:9:#                           learning rate tuned for the 16 K-param logistic baseline.\nconfigs/config_wave_full.yaml:149:  # 0.01 (the value config_script.yaml uses for the logistic baseline) DIVERGES Surya:\nADAPTING.md:24:\u251c\u2500\u2500 1_baseline_template.ipynb\nADAPTING.md:31:\u2502   \u2514\u2500\u2500 pl_simple_baseline.py        \u2190 FlareLightningModule (Lightning wrapper)\nADAPTING.md:35:    \u2514\u2500\u2500 simple_baseline.py           \u2190 RegressionFlareModel (linear baseline)\nADAPTING.md:114:> that is what `destandardize_channels()` gives the linear baseline, and it is usually what\nADAPTING.md:229:class in `models/` following the `RegressionFlareModel` pattern in `simple_baseline.py`.\nADAPTING.md:351:# Reproducible run, for comparing a change against a baseline (~20% slower)\nShell cwd was reset to /home/jovyan/surya_workshop2026/downstream_apps/test/experiments",
