les at lr=0.01: train loss 0.726 -> 0.0065, train\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/run_baseline_study.py:74:def fit_logistic(\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/run_baseline_study.py:233:            fit = fit_logistic(Xtr[idx], ytr[idx], Xva, yva,\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/run_baseline_study.py:264:            fit = fit_logistic(Xtr[idx], ytr[idx], Xva, yva, epochs=args.epochs,\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/run_baseline_study.py:285:            fit = fit_logistic(Xk[idx], ytr[idx], Xvk, yva, epochs=args.epochs,\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/run_baseline_study.py:334:    fit = fit_logistic(Xr, yr, Xva, yva, epochs=15, lr=args.lr, seed=42, batch_size=2)\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/extract_baseline_features.py:28:baseline's 32 (128x128, 64 KB/sample). Mean pooling composes exactly \u2014 pooling a\ndownstream_apps/test/4_finetune_wave_1D.py:97:                   help=\"Train the AIA193 running-difference logistic baseline instead of \"\ndownstream_apps/test/4_finetune_wave_1D.py:111:                        \"the 16 K-param logistic baseline and DIVERGES Surya.\")\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/README.md:4:running-difference logistic baseline, and does either improve as more images are used?\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/run_surya_schedule.sh:12:# had been tuned on the 16 K-parameter logistic baseline. The probe keeps the largest LR\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/wave_visibility_scan.py:24:* ``pooled_max`` \u2014 max \\\\|RD\\\\| of the 32x32-mean-pooled 128x128 map. This is the one that\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/wave_visibility_scan.py:25:  matters for the baseline, because it is literally a feature the logistic model sees.\ndownstream_apps/test/experiments/wave_visibility_scan.py:295:        [\"99.9th pct of |RD|\", \"std of RD\", \"max |RD| of the 128x128 pooled map\"],"
