            "raw_output": "63:class waveDSDatasetInMemory(waveDSDataset):\n77:            point of this class is that the configured ``s3_cache_dir`` is not.\n90:    def __init__(\n116:        # (the parent class builds a fresh client per download, which costs a TLS\n127:    def __getstate__(self):\n141:    def __setstate__(self, state):\n149:    def _get_client(self):\n189:    def _reset_client(self) -> None:\n202:    def _transfer_config(self):\n216:    def _local_cache_path(self, s3_uri: str) -> str:\n220:    def _cache_dir_bytes(self) -> int:\n227:    def _fetch_to_memory(self, s3_uri: str) -> io.BytesIO:\n250:            def _download() -> None:\n280:    def _maybe_write_cache(self, s3_uri: str, buf: io.BytesIO) -> None:\n300:    def load_nc_data(self, filepath: str, timestep, channels: list[str]) -> np.ndarray:\n===BUILDERS===\n79:def build_helio_datasets(\n80-    cfg,\n81-    dataset_cls: Type[Dataset],\n82-    scalers: Any = None,\n83-    **task_kwargs,\n84-) -> Tuple[Dataset, Dataset]:\n85-    \"\"\"Build the train and validation datasets described by ``cfg``.\n86-\n87-    Args:\n88-        cfg: A ``TrainingConfig`` from ``load_config()``.\n89-        dataset_cls: ``HelioNetCDFDataset`` or a subclass of it.\n90-        scalers: Normalization statistics. Built from ``cfg.data.scalers_path`` if omitted;\n91-            pass an existing dict to avoid re-reading the YAML.\n92-        **task_kwargs: Extra keyword arguments forwarded to ``dataset_cls`` \u2014 the\n93-            task-specific parameters your subclass adds.\n94-\n95-    Returns:\n96-        ``(train_dataset, val_dataset)``. They differ only in the index they read and in\n97-        ``phase``: the validation set uses ``phase=\"val\"``, which disables the random\n98-        channel masking and vertical flips that are applied during training.\n99-    \"\"\"\n100-    if scalers is None:\n101-        scalers = build_scalers(info=cfg.data.scalers_path)\n102-\n103-    common = {**_base_dataset_kwargs(cfg, scalers), **task_kwargs}\n104-\n105-    train_dataset = dataset_cls(index_path=cfg.data.train_data_path, phase=\"train\", **common)\n106-    val_dataset = dataset_cls(index_path=cfg.data.valid_data_path, phase=\"val\", **common)\n107-    return train_dataset, val_dataset\n108-\n109-\n110-def build_helio_dataloaders(\n111-    cfg,\n112-    dataset_cls: Type[Dataset],\n113-    scalers: Any = None,\n114-    num_workers: int | None = None,\n115-    seed: int | None = None,\n116-    **task_kwargs,\n117-) -> Tuple[DataLoader, DataLoader]:\n118-    \"\"\"Build the train and validation DataLoaders described by ``cfg``.\n119-\n120-    Args:\n121-        cfg: A ``TrainingConfig`` from ``load_config()``.\n122-        dataset_cls: ``HelioNetCDFDataset`` or a subclass of it.\n123-        scalers: Normalization statistics; built from the config if omitted.\n124-        num_workers: Override for ``cfg.num_workers`` (useful in notebooks, where fewer\n125-            workers start faster).\n126-        seed: Seed for the shuffle order and the per-worker RNGs. Defaults to ``cfg.seed``.\n127-            Pinning it explicitly is what makes the epoch order depend only on the config:\n128-            a bare ``shuffle=True`` seeds its sampler from whatever the global torch RNG\n129-            state happens to be when the iterator is created, so anything that consumes\n130-            RNG earlier in the program silently reshuffles the data.\n131-        **task_kwargs: Extra keyword arguments forwarded to ``dataset_cls``.\n132-\n133-    Returns:\n134-        ``(train_loader, val_loader)``. Only the training loader shuffles.\n135-    \"\"\"\n136-    train_dataset, val_dataset = build_helio_datasets(\n137-        cfg, dataset_cls, scalers=scalers, **task_kwargs\n138-    )\n139-",
