            "title": "cd workshop_infrastructure && grep -n \"def _base_dataset_kwargs\" -A 40 datasets/builders.py; echo \"===SCALERS===\"; sed -n '158,235p' utils.py | cat -n | awk '{printf \"%d\\t%s\\n\", NR+157, substr($0, index($0,\"\\t\")+1)}'",
            "tool_call_id": "toolu_bdrk_01Jdb27D5t1uzBuMZ9NbwiDo",
            "raw_output": "52:def _base_dataset_kwargs(cfg, scalers) -> dict:\n53-    \"\"\"Map a TrainingConfig onto the HelioNetCDFDataset constructor arguments.\n54-\n55-    This is the single place where config field names meet dataset parameter names.\n56-    \"\"\"\n57-    return dict(\n58-        # Temporal sampling\n59-        time_delta_input_minutes=cfg.data.time_delta_input_minutes,\n60-        time_delta_target_minutes=cfg.data.time_delta_target_minutes,\n61-        n_input_timestamps=cfg.model.time_embedding.time_dim,\n62-        rollout_steps=cfg.rollout_steps,\n63-        # Channels and normalization\n64-        channels=cfg.data.channels,\n65-        scalers=scalers,\n66-        # Augmentation\n67-        drop_hmi_probability=cfg.drop_hmi_probability,\n68-        use_latitude_in_learned_flow=cfg.use_latitude_in_learned_flow,\n69-        # Storage: local root, and how s3:// paths in the index are read\n70-        sdo_data_root_path=cfg.data.sdo_data_root_path,\n71-        s3_mode=cfg.data.s3_mode,\n72-        s3_storage_options={\"anon\": cfg.data.s3_anon},\n73-        s3_cache_dir=cfg.data.s3_cache_dir,\n74-        s3_boto3_max_concurrency=cfg.data.s3_boto3_max_concurrency,\n75-        s3_boto3_part_size_mb=cfg.data.s3_boto3_part_size_mb,\n76-    )\n77-\n78-\n79-def build_helio_datasets(\n80-    cfg,\n81-    dataset_cls: Type[Dataset],\n82-    scalers: Any = None,\n83-    **task_kwargs,\n84-) -> Tuple[Dataset, Dataset]:\n85-    \"\"\"Build the train and validation datasets described by ``cfg``.\n86-\n87-    Args:\n88-        cfg: A ``TrainingConfig`` from ``load_config()``.\n89-        dataset_cls: ``HelioNetCDFDataset`` or a subclass of it.\n90-        scalers: Normalization statistics. Built from ``cfg.data.scalers_path`` if omitted;\n91-            pass an existing dict to avoid re-reading the YAML.\n92-        **task_kwargs: Extra keyword arguments forwarded to ``dataset_cls`` \u2014 the\n===SCALERS===\n158\tdef build_scalers(info) -> Dict:\n159\t    \"\"\"Reconstruct per-channel scaler objects from a scalers YAML file or dict.\n160\t\n161\t    Args:\n162\t        info: Path to a scalers YAML file, or an already-loaded dict mapping\n163\t            channel name -> scaler parameters.\n164\t\n165\t    Returns:\n166\t        Dict mapping channel name -> scaler instance (e.g. ``StandardScaler``), each\n167\t        exposing ``.mean``, ``.std``, ``.epsilon`` and ``.sl_scale_factor``.\n168\t\n169\t    On the ``base:`` field\n170\t    ---------------------\n171\t    Every entry records the module the scaler was originally fitted in \u2014 in the\n172\t    shipped ``scalers.yaml`` that is ``surya.datasets.transformations``, which does not\n173\t    exist in this repo (the Surya code is vendored under ``workshop_infrastructure/``).\n174\t\n175\t    That field is deliberately **ignored**. Classes are always resolved from\n176\t    ``workshop_infrastructure.datasets.transformations``, never imported from the\n177\t    recorded path, so normalization does not depend on what happens to be installed in\n178\t    the environment: were a real ``surya`` package ever added, honoring ``base`` would\n179\t    silently switch which ``StandardScaler`` implementation runs, and results could move\n180\t    because of an unrelated install. Determinism matters more here than deference to a\n181\t    stale field. This is not warned about at runtime \u2014 the field is stale in every entry\n182\t    of a file fetched from HuggingFace that nobody can edit, so a warning would fire\n183\t    always and invite no action.\n184\t    \"\"\"\n185\t    import yaml\n186\t    import workshop_infrastructure.datasets.transformations as _transformations\n187\t\n188\t    source = \"<dict>\"\n189\t    if not isinstance(info, dict):\n190\t        source = str(info)\n191\t        if not os.path.isfile(source):\n192\t            raise FileNotFoundError(\n193\t                f\"Scalers file not found: {source}\\n\"\n194\t                \"This is the data.scalers_path entry in your config. It is downloaded \"\n195\t                \"automatically on the first run; to fetch it explicitly:\\n\"\n196\t                \"    python -m workshop_infrastructure.assets --scalers --dest <assets dir>\"\n197\t            )\n198\t        with open(source, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n199\t            info = yaml.safe_load(f)\n200\t\n201\t    if not isinstance(info, dict):\n202\t        raise ValueError(f\"Scalers source {source} must contain a mapping of channel name -> parameters.\")\n203\t\n204\t    available = sorted(\n205\t        name for name in dir(_transformations)\n206\t        if isinstance(getattr(_transformations, name), type)\n207\t    )\n208\t\n209\t    ret_dict = {}\n210\t    for p_key, p_val in info.items():\n211\t        if not isinstance(p_val, dict) or \"class\" not in p_val:\n212\t            raise ValueError(\n213\t                f\"Scalers entry {p_key!r} in {source} is malformed: expected a mapping \"\n214\t                f\"with a 'class' key, got {type(p_val).__name__}.\"\n215\t            )\n216\t        class_name = p_val[\"class\"]\n217\t        # Note: p_val[\"base\"] is intentionally not consulted \u2014 see the docstring.\n218\t        if not hasattr(_transformations, class_name):\n219\t            raise ValueError(\n220\t                f\"Scalers entry {p_key!r} in {source} names class {class_name!r}, which does \"\n221\t                \"not exist in workshop_infrastructure.datasets.transformations.\\n\"\n222\t                f\"Available classes: {', '.join(available)}.\"\n223\t            )\n224\t        ret_dict[p_key] = getattr(_transformations, class_name).from_dict(p_val)\n225\t    return ret_dict\n226\t\n227\t\n228\tHEAD_PREFIX = \"head_\"\n229\t\n230\t\n231\tdef discover_head_modules(model: torch.nn.Module) -> list[str]:\n232\t    \"\"\"Find the fine-tuning head modules to keep trainable under LoRA.\n233\t\n234\t    Convention: every trainable component of a fine-tuning head is a **direct\n235\t    child** of the top-level model whose attribute name starts with ``head_``",
            "kind": "execute",
